{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the people scattered throughout all the land of Egypt.</b> Because the Egyptians were destined to be struck, and perhaps the common people would say: why are we being struck, what is our offense against them? Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, put it into Pharaoh's heart to issue this decree, and the Israelites would gather straw and come and beat and strike them — even the maidservants and slaves — and therefore all of them were struck. <b>Straw for stubble.</b> In place of stubble they would gather straw to make the work from it, as in 'and their mortar became mortar for them' (i.e., one thing served in place of another)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:16.827430382Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}